      "question": "My manager wants a quick look at the oil condition on Transformer 1 at site MAIN. From the latest reading and the stats over the full available window, give me dielectric_rigidity, interfacial_v, oxygen, nitrogen and dbds, and say whether any of them moved in a direction that points to moisture ingress, air ingress or oil ageing. Rank the three concerns from most to least supported by the data. Don't use the combustible gases for this. If dielectric_rigidity or interfacial_v has no data, say so and base the ranking on oxygen and nitrogen only.",
      "answer": "**Transformer 1 \u2014 MAIN**  \nFull available window: **15\u201319 January 2024**, five readings per field, none missing. Latest: **19 January 2024, 00:00 UTC**\u2014historical, not current.\n\n| Measurement | Latest | Mean | Min\u2013max | Std. dev. | First\u2192latest change |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| dielectric_rigidity | 55 | 54.6 | 53\u201356 | 1.02 | 0 |\n| interfacial_v | 45 | 45 | 44\u201346 | 0.63 | 0 |\n| oxygen | 5,850 | 5,822 | 5,700\u20135,900 | 68.82 | \u221210 |\n| nitrogen | 27,850 | 27,868.4 | 27,700\u201328,000 | 103.32 | +8 |\n| dbds | 19 | 19 | 18\u201320 | 0.63 | 0 |\n\n*Units were not supplied by the data source.*\n\n**Concern ranking: all three tied\u2014no sustained directional support.**\n- **Moisture ingress:** dielectric rigidity dipped temporarily but recovered; no net deterioration.\n- **Air ingress:** oxygen and nitrogen did not rise together; their net changes were negligible.\n- **Oil ageing:** interfacial tension dipped temporarily but recovered, with no net decline. DBDS was unchanged overall and is primarily a corrosive-sulfur indicator, not direct evidence of ageing.\n\nThese five historical samples do not justify distinguishing the concerns by likelihood or ruling them out. No combustible gases were used.",
